<p>The only thing that strikes me as off, is the definition of the crimes the shadows react to. Mostly it has to do with the fact that each shadow is associated with a different era, and possibly a location within that era.</p>
<p>It might have been better to write it out describing that the shadows reacted to what would have been considered crimes of the eras and locations that they are depicted as coming from. Granted, you covered the general cases which would have been considered crimes in most, if not all societies, regardless of era and location.</p>

