					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/das-epos-sachs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1407410); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1407410&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609040570" alt="das Epos Sachs" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1407410)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/das-epos-sachs" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1407410); return false;" >das Epos Sachs</a></span> <span class="odate time_1343516953 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Jul 2012 23:09</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1521353">
									

<p>I like this. That said, I feel there are a few issues that could be addressed.</p>
<ul>
<li>Why are the containment rooms lit? A dark room throws no shadows. Or can the SCP-1002-XA instance manifest even in the dark?</li>
<li>If the SCP-1002-XA instance manifests when a target enters a 10m perimeter of SCP-1002-X then why is the smaller containment room 6mx6m? Surely the Foundation has the resources to make the room 12mx12m and contain the items in the central 2mx2m.</li>
<li>If a 10m breach of perimeter is required for SCP-1002-XA to manifest, and it <em>pursues</em> a target, how is it catching people? Remarkable agility is one thing, but if I see a dark shadowy humanoid manifest 9.5m in front of me, the first thing I'm going to do is take a step back. Maybe the SCP-1002-XA instances need to warp to individual?</li>
</ul>
<p>I also second the earlier suggestion of rewriting the crimes/punishments as a test log.</p>

							</div>

								
					
